//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// EmpModel [Pro+]
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Empirical Profile and Expansion Model [Pro+], placed in one script.
//
// Both are carried over verbatim. Neither model's logic, inputs, defaults,
// drawings, tables or alerts were altered. The only edits are the three renames
// forced by putting them in one namespace:
//
//     labelSize -> lvlLabelSize                       (Empirical Profile)
//         Both scripts declared a `labelSize`. The Profile's is a computed size
//         constant and the Model's is an input, so the Profile's was renamed as
//         the smaller edit.
//
//     up, dw, eq -> emUp, emDw, emEq                  (Expansion Model)
//         The Model's bar-direction globals would otherwise be shadowed by the
//         `bool up` parameter the Profile uses throughout its level maths.
//
//     tf -> tfStr, in tfLabel/tfMins only             (Expansion Model)
//         The Profile has a global `tf` that these two parameters would shadow.
//
// The two halves stay independent. Each keeps its own timeframe selector (the
// Profile's Projection Timeframe, the Model's Fractal), its own period
// detection, its own table and its own alert toggle. Pointing them at the same
// timeframe is a choice made in the settings, not one made here.
//
// WHAT SHARING ONE SCRIPT COSTS, since it cannot be renamed away:
//   * Drawing budget. Lines, labels and boxes cap at 500 EACH for the script as
//     a whole, and the two halves now draw from the same allowance. If maps stop
//     appearing, lower "Historical Periods to Show" or "HTF Candles".
//   * Load time. Nine request.security calls run here, eight of them the
//     Profile's. Disable feed pooling and the extra confluence timeframes first.
//
// Chart timeframe: the Profile wants a chart EQUAL TO OR FINER THAN its
// projection timeframe; the Model wants one at or below its fractal's lower
// timeframe. Each says so in its own table when it is not getting it.
// =============================================================================

// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// © staticdotsol

indicator("EmpModel [Pro+]", shorttitle="EmpModel", overlay=true,
     max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500)

// #############################################################################
// ##  PART 1 OF 2 - EMPIRICAL PROFILE                                        ##
// #############################################################################

// =============================================================================
// Empirical Profile (CRYPTO)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Anchors to each period's OPEN (4H/1D/1W/1M/1Y) and projects statistical
// levels around it, derived from the deepest higher-timeframe history the
// data provider allows:
//     * Manipulation (M) = the counter-trend excursion (liquidity / stop-hunt)
//     * Distribution (D) = the in-trend expansion       (profit targets)
//
// WHAT MAKES THIS "ADAPTIVE" (vs. a flat average of raw percentages):
//
//  1. VOLATILITY NORMALIZATION. Raw percentages mix regimes: 2011 BTC wicked
//     10%+ per day, 2024 BTC wicks ~2%. Averaging them describes the regime
//     mix, not tomorrow. In "Log + ATR" mode each period is stored as
//     excursion / ATR%-prevailing-at-that-time (a dimensionless "how many
//     ATRs did it wick"), then projected with TODAY's ATR%. This is what
//     makes a 5,000-period sample genuinely usable instead of merely large.
//
//  2. ASYMMETRY. Up and down excursions are not mirror images. Four separate
//     statistics are tracked (+M, -M, +D, -D) instead of one number mirrored.
//
//  3. PERCENTILES. Mean and median both answer "what is typical". A percentile
//     answers "only X% of periods extend past here" — an actual probability
//     attached to a target.
//
//  4. RECENCY WEIGHTING. Optional exponential half-life so recent periods
//     dominate without discarding the tail.
//
//  5. CONTEXT CONDITIONING. Optionally restrict the sample to periods sharing
//     today's context: same weekday, similar prior-period range, or similar
//     opening gap. Range expansion clusters, so this is not cosmetic.
//
//  6. HONEST SAMPLING. Standard errors are shown next to every ratio, the
//     table turns amber below the minimum-sample threshold, and reach/hold
//     rates are measured strictly walk-forward (each period judged only
//     against estimates built from periods BEFORE it) over the same rolling
//     window as the ratios themselves.
//
// DATA SOURCE:
//   Defaults to YOUR CHART SYMBOL, requested at the projection timeframe, so
//   it works identically on OKX, Kraken, MEXC, Coinbase, Bitstamp or anywhere
//   else with zero setup. Optionally override with a longer-history feed and
//   pool up to two more. Long BTC feeds: BITSTAMP:BTCUSD (2011+),
//   KRAKEN:BTCUSD (2013+), COINBASE:BTCUSD (2015+), CRYPTO:BTCUSD (index).
//   Ratios are dimensionless or percentage based, so whichever provider
//   supplies them they are always applied to YOUR chart symbol's open.
//
// PERFORMANCE NOTE: every enabled feed and every extra confluence timeframe
//   costs one request.security call, and Pine executes all of them whether or
//   not you use the result. Context conditioning and recency weighting both
//   add per-recompute work. If load time gets slow, disable pooling and extra
//   timeframes first.
//
// NOTE: run this on a chart timeframe EQUAL TO OR FINER THAN the projection
//   timeframe (view 5m/15m/1H while projecting 1D or 1W, etc).
//
// PRESENTATION: the map is drawn in the same visual language as
//   ohlc-statistical-mapping.pine (OHLC Statistical Mapping Pro+), so the two
//   read alike side by side — neutral level colours against an orange open,
//   transparent-background labels naming the timeframe, level and price, an
//   optional standard-deviation Zones mode, vertical phase-time markers,
//   completed periods faded rather than deleted, and a compact light table
//   laid out top of the map to the bottom (+DIS, +MAN, OPEN, -MAN, -DIS).
//
//   MANIPULATION SIGNS FOLLOW PRO+. A manipulation level is named for the
//   close direction of the periods it was sampled from, not for the side of
//   the open it sits on. An up-closing period sweeps the lows first, so
//   "+ Manipulation" is the level BELOW the open and "- Manipulation" the one
//   above. Distribution keeps reading geometrically — +D above, -D below —
//   because for distribution the two conventions agree.
//
//   Only the naming changed. Every level is computed, drawn and scored exactly
//   as before: the line that was labelled +M is the same line, now labelled -M.
// =============================================================================

// ================================== Inputs ===================================
grpP        = "Projection"
tfSel       = input.string("1D", "Projection Timeframe", options=["4H","1D","1W","1M","1Y"], group=grpP)
periodsShow = input.int(2,    "Historical Periods to Show", minval=1, maxval=20, group=grpP)
sampleLen   = input.int(2000, "Sample Size (completed periods)", minval=20, maxval=5000, group=grpP, tooltip="Rolling window of completed periods used for every statistic, including reach/hold rates. Leave high to use the most history possible.")

grpMod   = "Statistical Model"
transform = input.string("Log + ATR", "Excursion measure", options=["Percent","Log","Log + ATR"], group=grpMod, tooltip="Percent: (high-open)/open. Simple, but distorts on huge multi-year price ranges and mixes volatility regimes.\n\nLog: ln(high/open). Makes up and down moves symmetric — matters on 1M/1Y and on assets spanning orders of magnitude.\n\nLog + ATR (recommended): stores each period as log-excursion divided by the ATR% prevailing at that time, then re-scales by today's ATR%. Makes old history comparable to today instead of dragging the average toward a dead regime.")
atrLen    = input.int(14, "ATR length (periods, on projection TF)", minval=2, maxval=200, group=grpMod, tooltip="Volatility yardstick used by the 'Log + ATR' measure. Measured on the projection timeframe, always from bars that closed BEFORE the period being measured.")
uncondMode = input.bool(false, "Unconditional excursion mode", group=grpMod, tooltip="OFF (default, conditional): the original M/D model. Manipulation is sampled from periods that closed AGAINST that side (a down-wick on a green period), distribution from periods that closed WITH it.\n\nON (unconditional): every period contributes its up excursion and its down excursion with no reference to how it closed. This removes the subtle mismatch that the conditional model is defined by the period's close — something you do not know at the open. In this mode M and D differ only by their percentile setting.")
pctM      = input.float(50, "Manipulation percentile", minval=1, maxval=99, step=5, group=grpMod, tooltip="Percentile of the manipulation distribution to draw. 50 = median. Read it as: this level is exceeded by (100 - p)% of periods.")
pctD      = input.float(80, "Distribution percentile", minval=1, maxval=99, step=5, group=grpMod, tooltip="Percentile of the distribution/expansion sample. 80 means only 20% of periods extend beyond this level — a target with a stated probability rather than an average.")
recOn     = input.bool(false, "Recency weighting (exponential)", group=grpMod, tooltip="Weight recent periods more heavily. Costs load time and trims the effective sample to about six half-lives, since older data carries under 2% weight.")
halfLife  = input.int(250, "Half-life (periods)", minval=10, maxval=2000, group=grpMod, tooltip="A period this far back counts half as much as the newest one.")
condMode  = input.string("None", "Condition sample on", options=["None","Weekday","Prior range tercile","Gap direction"], group=grpMod, tooltip="Restrict the sample to periods sharing the current period's context.\n\nWeekday: Monday behaves differently from Friday (use on 4H/1D only).\nPrior range tercile: range expansion clusters — after a compressed period the next one expands.\nGap direction: for gapping markets, an up-gap open is a different animal from a flat one.\n\nConditioning splits the sample, so watch the n column and the amber warning.")
minSample = input.int(30, "Minimum sample per level", minval=5, maxval=500, group=grpMod, tooltip="Below this the table turns amber and reach/hold measurement stays in burn-in. A 1Y projection will often sit under this permanently — that is the honest answer, not a bug.")

grpS   = "Historical Data Source"
useCustomFeed = input.bool(false, "Override with a custom history feed", group=grpS, tooltip="OFF (default) = build stats from YOUR chart symbol's own higher-timeframe history. Works the same on any exchange, no setup. ON = borrow history from the feed below.")
sym1   = input.symbol("BITSTAMP:BTCUSD", "Custom history feed", group=grpS)
use2   = input.bool(false, "Pool extra feed #2", group=grpS, tooltip="Point it at the SAME asset on another exchange. Periods overlap in time, so pooling smooths exchange-specific wicks rather than extending history.")
sym2   = input.symbol("COINBASE:BTCUSD", "Extra feed #2", group=grpS)
use3   = input.bool(false, "Pool extra feed #3", group=grpS)
sym3   = input.symbol("KRAKEN:BTCUSD", "Extra feed #3", group=grpS)

grpC   = "Confluence (extra timeframes)"
cf2On  = input.bool(false, "Overlay timeframe #2", group=grpC, tooltip="Draws the current period's levels for a second timeframe and highlights where they cluster with the primary. Where a daily D level sits on a weekly M level is where reactions concentrate.")
cf2Tf  = input.string("1W", "Timeframe #2", options=["4H","1D","1W","1M","1Y"], group=grpC)
cf3On  = input.bool(false, "Overlay timeframe #3", group=grpC)
cf3Tf  = input.string("1M", "Timeframe #3", options=["4H","1D","1W","1M","1Y"], group=grpC)
cfTol  = input.float(0.25, "Confluence tolerance (%)", minval=0.01, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=grpC)
cfCol  = input.color(color.new(color.yellow, 80), "Confluence shading", group=grpC)

grpM   = "Manipulation (wick / liquidity)"
showM  = input.bool(true,  "Show Manipulation levels", group=grpM)
colM   = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 20), "Color", group=grpM)

grpD   = "Distribution (targets)"
showD  = input.bool(true,  "Show Distribution levels", group=grpD)
colD   = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 20), "Color", group=grpD)

grpO      = "Levels & Style"
drawMode  = input.string("Lines", "Draw levels as", options=["Lines","Zones"], group=grpO, tooltip="Zones widen the median level into a band of +/- a multiple of the sample's standard deviation, which is a more honest picture of where the estimate actually lives. The band uses the same standard deviation already reported as ±SE in the table, so nothing new is calculated.")
bandMult  = input.float(0.5, "Zone width (std deviations)", minval=0.05, maxval=3.0, step=0.05, group=grpO)
medStyleIn = input.string("Dashed", "Median line style", options=["Dotted","Dashed","Solid"], group=grpO, tooltip="Mean always draws solid and the percentile always draws dotted, so the three statistics stay distinguishable. This picks the style of the median line between them.")
lnWidth   = input.int(1, "Line width", minval=1, maxval=4, group=grpO)
showMean  = input.bool(true, "Draw mean lines", group=grpO)
showMed   = input.bool(true, "Draw median lines", group=grpO)
showPct   = input.bool(true, "Draw percentile lines", group=grpO)
showFill  = input.bool(true, "Shade mean-median zones", group=grpO)
showO     = input.bool(true, "Show open (accumulation) line", group=grpO, inline="op")
colO      = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 30), "", group=grpO, inline="op")
lblMode   = input.string("Long", "Labels", options=["Long","Short","None"], group=grpO, tooltip="Long: '1D / + Distribution'. Short: '1D + D'. The statistic each line carries is appended as mu, ~ or pNN.")
lblSize   = input.string("tiny", "Label size", options=["tiny","small","normal"], group=grpO)
histDim   = input.bool(true, "Dim completed periods", group=grpO, tooltip="Fades the maps of periods that have already closed so the running period reads first, while the record of what was projected stays on the chart.")

grpW     = "Projection Width"
extendTo = input.string("Period end", "Extend levels to", options=["Period end","Last bar","Fixed bars"], group=grpW)
extBars  = input.int(40, "Fixed bars", minval=1, maxval=500, group=grpW)

grpTm     = "Timing"
showTime  = input.bool(true, "Project average phase times", group=grpTm, tooltip="Vertical markers at the average point inside the period where each phase has historically completed. The manipulation marker spans the two manipulation levels; the high and low markers span the two distribution levels. These read the same walk-forward accumulators as the table's Timing row, so they add no calculation.")
colTime   = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 35), "Marker colour", group=grpTm)
showTimeL = input.bool(true, "Show time labels", group=grpTm)

grpT     = "Table"
showTbl  = input.bool(true, "Show statistics table", group=grpT)
showSeq  = input.bool(true, "Show sequencing & timing rows", group=grpT, tooltip="Measured on the CHART timeframe (the only place intra-period order is visible), so it carries its own smaller sample size. It answers the model's core claim: does the manipulation side actually get swept BEFORE the distribution target, and when in the period do the extremes print?")
showRange = input.bool(false, "Add average-range row", group=grpT, tooltip="Typical candle range implied by the median levels, averaged over the up-close case (lower manipulation to upper distribution) and the down-close case (upper manipulation to lower distribution).")
tblPos   = input.string("bottom_center", "Position", options=["bottom_center","bottom_left","bottom_right","top_center","top_left","top_right","middle_left","middle_right"], group=grpT)
tblSize  = input.string("tiny", "Text size", options=["auto","tiny","small","normal"], group=grpT)
tblTxtCol = input.color(color.new(color.black, 0), "Text colour", group=grpT)
tblBgCol  = input.color(color.new(color.white, 20), "Background", group=grpT)

grpA     = "Alerts"
alertOn  = input.bool(true, "Enable alert() calls", group=grpA, tooltip="Fires on first tag of each level in a period, and on the close-back-through that actually confirms a manipulation.")

// map selection to a timeframe string  (Year = "12M" in TradingView)
f_tf(string s) => s == "4H" ? "240" : s == "1W" ? "1W" : s == "1M" ? "1M" : s == "1Y" ? "12M" : "1D"
tf  = f_tf(tfSel)
tfB = f_tf(cf2Tf)
tfC = f_tf(cf3Tf)

// number of context buckets implied by the conditioning mode
nBuckets = condMode == "Weekday" ? 7 : condMode == "None" ? 1 : 3

// ============================ Presentation helpers ============================
medStyle  = medStyleIn == "Solid" ? line.style_solid : medStyleIn == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_dashed
lvlLabelSize = lblSize == "small" ? size.small : lblSize == "normal" ? size.normal : size.tiny

// Drawings are positioned in TIME, not bar index. A monthly projection on a
// 15m chart is ~2,880 bars long, and objects placed with xloc.bar_index cannot
// be drawn more than 500 bars into the future — xloc.bar_time has no such
// limit, so the period-end projection works on every timeframe pair.
chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
barMs    = chartSec * 1000
periodMs = float(timeframe.in_seconds(tf)) * 1000.0
// Initial width of a freshly drawn level, before the per-bar extend below.
projMs   = extendTo == "Fixed bars" ? extBars * barMs : int(periodMs)
// Confluence shading still works in bar index, so it keeps the 500-bar cap the
// old projection-width input enforced.
cfBars   = math.min(500, extendTo == "Fixed bars" ? extBars : math.max(1, int(math.round(periodMs / 1000.0 / math.max(1, chartSec)))))

// Level ordering, top of the map to the bottom. Also the table's row order.
// 0 = +D, 1 = -M, 2 = Open, 3 = +M, 4 = -D.
//
// The MANIPULATION sign names the close direction of the sessions it was
// sampled from, not the side of the open it sits on: an up-closing period
// sweeps the lows first, so "+ Manipulation" is the level BELOW the open and
// "- Manipulation" the one above. This matches OHLC Statistical Mapping Pro+.
// The DISTRIBUTION sign still reads geometrically, +D above and -D below,
// because there the two conventions agree, which is this script's convention throughout.
f_levelName(int i, bool shortForm) =>
    switch i
        0 => shortForm ? "+ D" : "+ Distribution"
        1 => shortForm ? "- M" : "- Manipulation"
        2 => shortForm ? "0"   : "Open"
        3 => shortForm ? "+ M" : "+ Manipulation"
        => shortForm ? "- D" : "- Distribution"

f_levelTag(int i) =>
    switch i
        0 => "+DIS"
        1 => "-MAN"
        2 => "OPEN"
        3 => "+MAN"
        => "-DIS"

// Label text: timeframe, level, which statistic this particular line is, and
// the price it projects to.
f_lblTxt(int i, string stat, float px) =>
    string s = stat == "" ? "" : "  " + stat
    string p = na(px) ? "" : "  " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick)
    lblMode == "Short" ? tfSel + " " + f_levelName(i, true) + s + p : tfSel + "\n" + f_levelName(i, false) + s + p

// Format a projected timestamp. Sub-daily periods want a clock, longer periods
// want a date — "14:35" on a monthly projection would be meaningless.
f_stamp(int ts) =>
    float periodMs = float(timeframe.in_seconds(tf)) * 1000.0
    string fmt = periodMs >= 432000000.0 ? "dd MMM" : periodMs >= 86400000.0 ? "dd HH:mm" : "HH:mm"
    str.format_time(ts, fmt, syminfo.timezone)

// ============================ Shared math helpers =============================
// Rebuild a price level from a stored ratio. Mirrors the excursion measure so
// that whatever transform went in comes back out as a price.
f_lvl(string tfm, float v, float o, float atrp, bool up) =>
    float r = na
    if not na(v) and not na(o)
        if tfm == "Percent"
            r := up ? o * (1.0 + v) : o * (1.0 - v)
        else if tfm == "Log"
            r := up ? o * math.exp(v) : o * math.exp(-v)
        else if not na(atrp)
            r := up ? o * math.exp(v * atrp) : o * math.exp(-v * atrp)
    r

// Exponentially weighted mean. Falls back to a plain average when weighting
// is off, which is the common path and stays on the native implementation.
f_wmean(array<float> vals, float hl) =>
    int n = array.size(vals)
    float res = na
    if n > 0
        if na(hl) or hl <= 0
            res := array.avg(vals)
        else
            float decay = math.pow(0.5, 1.0 / hl)
            float sw = 0.0
            float sv = 0.0
            for i = 0 to n - 1
                float w = math.pow(decay, n - 1 - i)
                sw += w
                sv += array.get(vals, i) * w
            res := sw > 0 ? sv / sw : na
    res

// Weighted percentile. Sorting is native; only the cumulative-weight walk is
// interpreted, and it exits as soon as the threshold is crossed.
f_wpct(array<float> vals, float hl, float pct) =>
    int n = array.size(vals)
    float res = na
    if n > 0
        if na(hl) or hl <= 0
            res := array.percentile_linear_interpolation(vals, pct)
        else
            float decay = math.pow(0.5, 1.0 / hl)
            float tot = decay >= 1.0 ? n : (1.0 - math.pow(decay, n)) / (1.0 - decay)
            array<int> idx = array.sort_indices(vals, order.ascending)
            float target = tot * pct / 100.0
            float cum = 0.0
            for k = 0 to n - 1
                int i = array.get(idx, k)
                cum += math.pow(decay, n - 1 - i)
                if cum >= target
                    res := array.get(vals, i)
                    break
            if na(res)
                res := array.get(vals, array.get(idx, n - 1))
    res

// Which context bucket does a period belong to?
f_bucket(string cond, int nb, float o, float prevC, float prevRange, float t1, float t2, float atrp, int tm) =>
    int b = 0
    if cond == "Weekday"
        b := dayofweek(tm) - 1
    else if cond == "Prior range tercile"
        b := na(t1) or na(prevRange) ? 1 : prevRange <= t1 ? 0 : prevRange <= t2 ? 1 : 2
    else if cond == "Gap direction"
        float g = na(prevC) or prevC == 0 ? 0.0 : (o - prevC) / prevC
        float th = na(atrp) ? 0.0 : 0.25 * atrp
        b := g < -th ? 0 : g > th ? 2 : 1
    math.max(0, math.min(nb - 1, b))

// ========================== Engine result container ===========================
// Only scalar fields cross the request.security boundary. Returning the sample
// arrays themselves copies thousands of floats per chart bar and exhausts
// Pine's memory budget — that is what this layout exists to avoid.
type Res
    float m0 = na
    float d0 = na
    float p0 = na
    float s0 = na
    float n0 = 0.0
    float m1 = na
    float d1 = na
    float p1 = na
    float s1 = na
    float n1 = 0.0
    float m2 = na
    float d2 = na
    float p2 = na
    float s2 = na
    float n2 = 0.0
    float m3 = na
    float d3 = na
    float p3 = na
    float s3 = na
    float n3 = 0.0
    float rd0 = na
    float hd0 = na
    float rp0 = na
    float hp0 = na
    float rd1 = na
    float hd1 = na
    float rp1 = na
    float hp1 = na
    float rd2 = na
    float hd2 = na
    float rp2 = na
    float hp2 = na
    float rd3 = na
    float hd3 = na
    float rp3 = na
    float hp3 = na
    float evalN = 0.0
    float bothR = na
    float atrP = na

// Rolling walk-forward outcome record for one (level, statistic) combination.
type Outcome
    array<float> reach
    array<float> held

// Write one role's statistics into the cache slot k.
f_store(array<float> cM, array<float> cD, array<float> cP, array<float> cS,
         array<float> cN, int k, array<float> f, float hl, float pct) =>
    int m = array.size(f)
    array.set(cN, k, m)
    if m >= 2
        array.set(cM, k, f_wmean(f, hl))
        array.set(cD, k, f_wpct(f, hl, 50.0))
        array.set(cP, k, f_wpct(f, hl, pct))
        array.set(cS, k, array.stdev(f, false))
    else
        array.set(cM, k, na)
        array.set(cD, k, na)
        array.set(cP, k, na)
        array.set(cS, k, na)

// Record one walk-forward outcome, trimmed to the same window as the ratios.
f_push(Outcome oc, bool reached, bool held, int maxN) =>
    array.push(oc.reach, reached ? 1.0 : 0.0)
    array.push(oc.held, held ? 1.0 : 0.0)
    if array.size(oc.reach) > maxN
        array.shift(oc.reach)
        array.shift(oc.held)

f_reachRate(Outcome oc) =>
    array.size(oc.reach) > 0 ? array.sum(oc.reach) / array.size(oc.reach) : na

f_holdRate(Outcome oc) =>
    float r = array.sum(oc.reach)
    r > 0 ? array.sum(oc.held) / r : na

// ================================= The engine =================================
// Runs INSIDE request.security at the projection timeframe, walking the
// provider's entire higher-timeframe history. Every period is read from bar[1]
// so only confirmed data enters the sample and nothing repaints.
//
// Role indices: 0 = +M (upper manipulation), 1 = -M (lower manipulation),
//               2 = +D (upper distribution), 3 = -D (lower distribution).
f_engine(int maxN, int aLen, string tfm, bool recOn_, float hl_, string cond,
         int nb, bool uncond, float pM, float pD, int minN, bool full) =>
    var array<float> upA = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> dnA = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> blA = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> bkA = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> rgA = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> cM  = array.new<float>(4 * nb, na)
    var array<float> cD  = array.new<float>(4 * nb, na)
    var array<float> cP  = array.new<float>(4 * nb, na)
    var array<float> cS  = array.new<float>(4 * nb, na)
    var array<float> cN  = array.new<float>(4 * nb, 0)
    var array<Outcome> ocs = array.new<Outcome>()
    // Scratch buffers for the recompute. Allocating these fresh on every
    // recompute churned thousands of 2000-element arrays per feed, which is
    // what exhausted memory; they are reused and cleared instead.
    var array<float> f0 = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> f1 = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> f2 = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> f3 = array.new<float>()
    var float terc1 = na
    var float terc2 = na
    var int sinceRe = 999
    var float bothN = 0.0
    var float bothHit = 0.0

    if array.size(ocs) == 0
        for j = 0 to 7
            array.push(ocs, Outcome.new(reach = array.new<float>(), held = array.new<float>()))

    // ta.atr must be evaluated on every bar, never inside a branch, or its
    // internal state desynchronises from the series.
    float atrSeries = ta.atr(aLen)

    float hl = na
    if recOn_
        hl := hl_
    // Beyond ~6 half-lives a period carries under 2% weight, so trimming there
    // costs nothing statistically and keeps the weighted walk bounded.
    int effMax = recOn_ ? int(math.min(maxN, math.round(hl_ * 6.0))) : maxN

    if bar_index > 1
        float o = open[1]
        float h = high[1]
        float l = low[1]
        float c = close[1]
        float pc = close[2]
        // Volatility yardstick known strictly BEFORE the period being measured.
        float atrPrev = close[2] > 0 ? atrSeries[2] / close[2] : na
        float prevRange = na(close[2]) or close[2] == 0 ? na : (high[2] - low[2]) / close[2]

        if o > 0 and h > 0 and l > 0
            // ---- excursions, in the selected measure ----
            float upV = tfm == "Percent" ? (h - o) / o : math.log(h / o)
            float dnV = tfm == "Percent" ? (o - l) / o : math.log(o / l)
            if tfm == "Log + ATR"
                if na(atrPrev) or atrPrev <= 0
                    upV := na
                    dnV := na
                else
                    upV := upV / atrPrev
                    dnV := dnV / atrPrev

            if not na(upV) and not na(dnV)
                int bk = f_bucket(cond, nb, o, pc, prevRange, terc1, terc2, atrPrev, time[1])
                int base = 4 * bk

                // ---- walk-forward scoring: judge this period against estimates
                // built only from periods that preceded it. Only the primary
                // feed needs this; pooled feeds contribute ratios alone, so
                // they skip it and keep their outcome buffers empty. ----
                if full
                    for r = 0 to 3
                        bool upSide = r == 0 or r == 2
                        if array.get(cN, base + r) >= minN
                            float vd = array.get(cD, base + r)
                            float vp = array.get(cP, base + r)
                            float ld = f_lvl(tfm, vd, o, atrPrev, upSide)
                            float lp = f_lvl(tfm, vp, o, atrPrev, upSide)
                            bool rd = upSide ? h >= ld : l <= ld
                            bool hd = rd and (upSide ? c < ld : c > ld)
                            bool rp = upSide ? h >= lp : l <= lp
                            bool hp = rp and (upSide ? c < lp : c > lp)
                            f_push(array.get(ocs, r), rd, hd, effMax)
                            f_push(array.get(ocs, 4 + r), rp, hp, effMax)

                // ---- whipsaw: how often BOTH manipulation sides get tagged ----
                if array.get(cN, base) >= minN and array.get(cN, base + 1) >= minN
                    float lu = f_lvl(tfm, array.get(cD, base), o, atrPrev, true)
                    float ldn = f_lvl(tfm, array.get(cD, base + 1), o, atrPrev, false)
                    bothN += 1.0
                    if h >= lu and l <= ldn
                        bothHit += 1.0

                // ---- record the period ----
                array.push(upA, upV)
                array.push(dnA, dnV)
                array.push(blA, c >= o ? 1.0 : 0.0)
                array.push(bkA, bk)
                if array.size(upA) > effMax
                    array.shift(upA)
                    array.shift(dnA)
                    array.shift(blA)
                    array.shift(bkA)
                if not na(prevRange)
                    array.push(rgA, prevRange)
                    if array.size(rgA) > 500
                        array.shift(rgA)

                // ---- throttled recompute of cached statistics ----
                // The estimate barely moves between adjacent periods once the
                // sample is large, so recomputing every bar is wasted work.
                int n = array.size(upA)
                sinceRe += 1
                int reEvery = n < 250 ? 1 : 25
                if sinceRe >= reEvery or barstate.islast
                    sinceRe := 0
                    if cond == "Prior range tercile" and array.size(rgA) >= 30
                        terc1 := array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rgA, 33.3333)
                        terc2 := array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rgA, 66.6667)
                    for b = 0 to nb - 1
                        array.clear(f0)
                        array.clear(f1)
                        array.clear(f2)
                        array.clear(f3)
                        // n is at least 1 here: the current period was just pushed
                        for i = 0 to n - 1
                            if nb == 1 or int(array.get(bkA, i)) == b
                                float u = array.get(upA, i)
                                float d = array.get(dnA, i)
                                if uncond
                                    array.push(f0, u)
                                    array.push(f1, d)
                                    array.push(f2, u)
                                    array.push(f3, d)
                                else if array.get(blA, i) > 0.5
                                    array.push(f1, d)
                                    array.push(f2, u)
                                else
                                    array.push(f0, u)
                                    array.push(f3, d)
                        f_store(cM, cD, cP, cS, cN, 4 * b + 0, f0, hl, pM)
                        f_store(cM, cD, cP, cS, cN, 4 * b + 1, f1, hl, pM)
                        f_store(cM, cD, cP, cS, cN, 4 * b + 2, f2, hl, pD)
                        f_store(cM, cD, cP, cS, cN, 4 * b + 3, f3, hl, pD)

    // ---- assemble the result for the period about to be projected ----
    float atrNow = close[1] > 0 ? atrSeries[1] / close[1] : na
    float pcNow = close[2]
    float rangeNow = na(close[2]) or close[2] == 0 ? na : (high[2] - low[2]) / close[2]
    int bkNow = f_bucket(cond, nb, open[1], pcNow, rangeNow, terc1, terc2, atrNow, time)
    int bn = 4 * bkNow

    Res out = Res.new()
    out.m0 := array.get(cM, bn + 0)
    out.d0 := array.get(cD, bn + 0)
    out.p0 := array.get(cP, bn + 0)
    out.s0 := array.get(cS, bn + 0)
    out.n0 := array.get(cN, bn + 0)
    out.m1 := array.get(cM, bn + 1)
    out.d1 := array.get(cD, bn + 1)
    out.p1 := array.get(cP, bn + 1)
    out.s1 := array.get(cS, bn + 1)
    out.n1 := array.get(cN, bn + 1)
    out.m2 := array.get(cM, bn + 2)
    out.d2 := array.get(cD, bn + 2)
    out.p2 := array.get(cP, bn + 2)
    out.s2 := array.get(cS, bn + 2)
    out.n2 := array.get(cN, bn + 2)
    out.m3 := array.get(cM, bn + 3)
    out.d3 := array.get(cD, bn + 3)
    out.p3 := array.get(cP, bn + 3)
    out.s3 := array.get(cS, bn + 3)
    out.n3 := array.get(cN, bn + 3)
    out.rd0 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 0))
    out.hd0 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 0))
    out.rd1 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 1))
    out.hd1 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 1))
    out.rd2 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 2))
    out.hd2 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 2))
    out.rd3 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 3))
    out.hd3 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 3))
    out.rp0 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 4))
    out.hp0 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 4))
    out.rp1 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 5))
    out.hp1 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 5))
    out.rp2 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 6))
    out.hp2 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 6))
    out.rp3 := f_reachRate(array.get(ocs, 7))
    out.hp3 := f_holdRate(array.get(ocs, 7))
    out.evalN := array.size(array.get(ocs, 0).reach)
    out.bothR := bothN > 0 ? bothHit / bothN : na
    out.atrP := atrNow
    out

// ============================== Feed requests =================================
statSym1 = useCustomFeed ? sym1 : syminfo.tickerid

s1 = request.security(statSym1, tf, f_engine(sampleLen, atrLen, transform, recOn, halfLife, condMode, nBuckets, uncondMode, pctM, pctD, minSample, true))
s2 = request.security(sym2,     tf, f_engine(sampleLen, atrLen, transform, recOn, halfLife, condMode, nBuckets, uncondMode, pctM, pctD, minSample, false))
s3 = request.security(sym3,     tf, f_engine(sampleLen, atrLen, transform, recOn, halfLife, condMode, nBuckets, uncondMode, pctM, pctD, minSample, false))

// Volatility scale is always taken from the CHART symbol, so ATR-normalized
// ratios borrowed from another provider land on the right absolute size here.
chartAtrP = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, ta.atr(atrLen)[1] / close[1])

// Extra timeframes for confluence use the primary feed only.
sB = request.security(statSym1, tfB, f_engine(sampleLen, atrLen, transform, recOn, halfLife, condMode, nBuckets, uncondMode, pctM, pctD, minSample, false))
sC = request.security(statSym1, tfC, f_engine(sampleLen, atrLen, transform, recOn, halfLife, condMode, nBuckets, uncondMode, pctM, pctD, minSample, false))
chartAtrB = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfB, ta.atr(atrLen)[1] / close[1])
chartAtrC = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfC, ta.atr(atrLen)[1] / close[1])

// A feed returns na for bars that predate its history — Coinbase has no 2011,
// SPY has no 1970 — and reading a field off an na object is a runtime error,
// not a silent na. Coarser charts reach further back, which is why this only
// bit above 4H. Substitute an empty result so a feed that does not reach this
// far back contributes nothing instead of taking the whole script down.
var Res EMPTY = Res.new()
e1 = na(s1) ? EMPTY : s1
e2 = na(s2) ? EMPTY : s2
e3 = na(s3) ? EMPTY : s3
eB = na(sB) ? EMPTY : sB
eC = na(sC) ? EMPTY : sC

// Projection must be at least as coarse as the chart, or period detection
// degenerates and every chart bar looks like a fresh period.
tfInverted = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) > timeframe.in_seconds(tf)

// =============================== Pooling ======================================
// Sample-size-weighted blend. For the mean this is exact; for median and
// percentile it is an approximation, which is acceptable because pooled feeds
// track the same asset and their quantiles sit close together.
f_pool(float a, float b, float c, float na_, float nb_, float nc_) =>
    float w1 = na(a) ? 0.0 : nz(na_)
    float w2 = use2 and not na(b) ? nz(nb_) : 0.0
    float w3 = use3 and not na(c) ? nz(nc_) : 0.0
    float tot = w1 + w2 + w3
    tot > 0 ? (nz(a) * w1 + nz(b) * w2 + nz(c) * w3) / tot : na

f_poolN(float a, float b, float c) =>
    nz(a) + (use2 ? nz(b) : 0.0) + (use3 ? nz(c) : 0.0)

// role 0 = +M, 1 = -M, 2 = +D, 3 = -D
n0 = f_poolN(e1.n0, e2.n0, e3.n0)
n1 = f_poolN(e1.n1, e2.n1, e3.n1)
n2 = f_poolN(e1.n2, e2.n2, e3.n2)
n3 = f_poolN(e1.n3, e2.n3, e3.n3)

mean0 = f_pool(e1.m0, e2.m0, e3.m0, e1.n0, e2.n0, e3.n0)
mean1 = f_pool(e1.m1, e2.m1, e3.m1, e1.n1, e2.n1, e3.n1)
mean2 = f_pool(e1.m2, e2.m2, e3.m2, e1.n2, e2.n2, e3.n2)
mean3 = f_pool(e1.m3, e2.m3, e3.m3, e1.n3, e2.n3, e3.n3)
med0  = f_pool(e1.d0, e2.d0, e3.d0, e1.n0, e2.n0, e3.n0)
med1  = f_pool(e1.d1, e2.d1, e3.d1, e1.n1, e2.n1, e3.n1)
med2  = f_pool(e1.d2, e2.d2, e3.d2, e1.n2, e2.n2, e3.n2)
med3  = f_pool(e1.d3, e2.d3, e3.d3, e1.n3, e2.n3, e3.n3)
pct0  = f_pool(e1.p0, e2.p0, e3.p0, e1.n0, e2.n0, e3.n0)
pct1  = f_pool(e1.p1, e2.p1, e3.p1, e1.n1, e2.n1, e3.n1)
pct2  = f_pool(e1.p2, e2.p2, e3.p2, e1.n2, e2.n2, e3.n2)
pct3  = f_pool(e1.p3, e2.p3, e3.p3, e1.n3, e2.n3, e3.n3)

// Standard error of the mean: sd / sqrt(n). The honest width of the estimate.
f_se(float sd, float n) => na(sd) or nz(n) < 2 ? na : sd / math.sqrt(n)
se0 = f_se(e1.s0, e1.n0)
se1 = f_se(e1.s1, e1.n1)
se2 = f_se(e1.s2, e1.n2)
se3 = f_se(e1.s3, e1.n3)

smallestN = math.min(math.min(n0, n1), math.min(n2, n3))
hasStats = smallestN >= 5
thin = smallestN < minSample

// ========================== Current period anchor =============================
// Levels are projected from YOUR chart symbol's open; only the ratios and the
// volatility scale come from the provider.
var float curO = na
var int   startTime = na
newP = ta.change(time(tf)) != 0
if newP
    curO := open
    startTime := time

appliedAtr = transform == "Log + ATR" ? chartAtrP : na

lvlPMm = f_lvl(transform, mean0, curO, appliedAtr, true)
lvlPMd = f_lvl(transform, med0,  curO, appliedAtr, true)
lvlPMp = f_lvl(transform, pct0,  curO, appliedAtr, true)
lvlNMm = f_lvl(transform, mean1, curO, appliedAtr, false)
lvlNMd = f_lvl(transform, med1,  curO, appliedAtr, false)
lvlNMp = f_lvl(transform, pct1,  curO, appliedAtr, false)
lvlPDm = f_lvl(transform, mean2, curO, appliedAtr, true)
lvlPDd = f_lvl(transform, med2,  curO, appliedAtr, true)
lvlPDp = f_lvl(transform, pct2,  curO, appliedAtr, true)
lvlNDm = f_lvl(transform, mean3, curO, appliedAtr, false)
lvlNDd = f_lvl(transform, med3,  curO, appliedAtr, false)
lvlNDp = f_lvl(transform, pct3,  curO, appliedAtr, false)

// ===================== Timing accumulators (chart TF) =========================
// Declared here rather than with the rest of the sequencing block below because
// the phase-time markers are drawn at the period open and read them. They are
// written to further down, so a marker drawn now reflects strictly completed
// periods — walk-forward, same as the table row it mirrors.
var float seqN     = 0.0
var float seqMwin  = 0.0
var float seqDwin  = 0.0
var float sumHiFr  = 0.0
var float sumLoFr  = 0.0
var float sumMFr   = 0.0
var float mFrN     = 0.0
var float extN     = 0.0

// ============================= Drawing helpers ================================
// Colours are carried alongside the drawings because Pine can read a line's
// coordinates back but not its colour, and a completed period has to be dimmed
// from whatever colour it was originally given.
type LevelGroup
    array<line>     lines
    array<color>    lineCols
    array<linefill> fills
    array<label>    labels
    array<color>    labelCols
    array<box>      boxes
    array<color>    boxCols

var array<LevelGroup> groups = array.new<LevelGroup>()
var LevelGroup active = na

f_newGroup() =>
    LevelGroup.new(array.new<line>(), array.new<color>(), array.new<linefill>(),
         array.new<label>(), array.new<color>(), array.new<box>(), array.new<color>())

// x is a TIMESTAMP throughout the drawing layer, not a bar index.
mkLine(int x, float y, color c, string st, int w) =>
    na(y) ? na : line.new(x, y, x + projMs, y, xloc=xloc.bar_time, color=c, style=st, width=w)

// Transparent-background label with coloured text, set left of its anchor.
mkLabel(int x, float y, string txt, color c) =>
    na(y) ? na : label.new(x, y, txt, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_left,
         color=color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor=c, size=lvlLabelSize, textalign=text.align_left)

f_add(LevelGroup g, line ln, color c) =>
    if not na(ln)
        array.push(g.lines, ln)
        array.push(g.lineCols, c)

f_addLbl(LevelGroup g, label lb, color c) =>
    if not na(lb)
        array.push(g.labels, lb)
        array.push(g.labelCols, c)

// Fade every drawing a group owns. Called on the previous period's group once a
// new period opens, so the running map reads first without losing the record.
f_dim(LevelGroup g) =>
    if not na(g)
        if array.size(g.lines) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(g.lines) - 1
                line.set_color(array.get(g.lines, i), color.new(array.get(g.lineCols, i), 70))
        if array.size(g.labels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(g.labels) - 1
                label.set_textcolor(array.get(g.labels, i), color.new(array.get(g.labelCols, i), 70))
        if array.size(g.boxes) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(g.boxes) - 1
                box.set_bgcolor(array.get(g.boxes, i), color.new(array.get(g.boxCols, i), 80))
    true

// Band edges for a Zones-mode level, built from the same standard deviation the
// table already reports as ±SE. The ratio is widened in ratio space and then
// converted to price, so the band respects the selected excursion measure.
// Two scalar calls rather than one tuple, since the caller is a local block.
f_bandHi(float ratio, float sd, bool up) =>
    na(ratio) or na(sd) or sd <= 0 ? float(na) : f_lvl(transform, ratio + bandMult * sd, curO, appliedAtr, up)

f_bandLo(float ratio, float sd, bool up) =>
    na(ratio) or na(sd) or sd <= 0 ? float(na) : f_lvl(transform, math.max(0.0, ratio - bandMult * sd), curO, appliedAtr, up)

// Draw one side of one level family: mean, median and percentile.
f_drawSet(LevelGroup g, int x, float vm, float vd, float vp, float bHi, float bLo, color col, int li) =>
    line lm = showMean ? mkLine(x, vm, col, line.style_solid, lnWidth) : na
    line ld = showMed ? mkLine(x, vd, col, medStyle, lnWidth) : na
    line lp = showPct ? mkLine(x, vp, col, line.style_dotted, lnWidth) : na
    f_add(g, lm, col)
    f_add(g, ld, col)
    f_add(g, lp, col)
    if drawMode == "Zones" and not na(bHi) and not na(bLo)
        array.push(g.boxes, box.new(x, math.max(bHi, bLo), x + projMs, math.min(bHi, bLo),
             xloc=xloc.bar_time, border_color=color.new(col, 100), bgcolor=color.new(col, 55)))
        array.push(g.boxCols, color.new(col, 55))
    else if showFill and not na(lm) and not na(ld)
        array.push(g.fills, linefill.new(lm, ld, color.new(col, 86)))
    if lblMode != "None"
        float pShown = (li == 1 or li == 3) ? pctM : pctD
        f_addLbl(g, showMean ? mkLabel(x, vm, f_lblTxt(li, "mu", vm), col) : na, col)
        f_addLbl(g, showMed ? mkLabel(x, vd, f_lblTxt(li, "~", vd), col) : na, col)
        f_addLbl(g, showPct ? mkLabel(x, vp, f_lblTxt(li, "p" + str.tostring(pShown, "#"), vp), col) : na, col)

// Vertical marker at the average point inside the period where a phase has
// historically completed, spanning the pair of levels it belongs to.
f_timeMark(LevelGroup g, int x0, float frac, float yA, float yB, string tag) =>
    if showTime and not na(frac) and not na(yA) and not na(yB)
        int xm = x0 + int(math.round(frac * periodMs))
        array.push(g.lines, line.new(xm, yA, xm, yB, xloc=xloc.bar_time, color=colTime, style=line.style_dotted, width=lnWidth))
        array.push(g.lineCols, colTime)
        if showTimeL
            label lb = label.new(xm, math.min(yA, yB), tag + " " + f_stamp(xm), xloc=xloc.bar_time,
                 style=label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.black, 100),
                 textcolor=colTime, size=lvlLabelSize)
            array.push(g.labels, lb)
            array.push(g.labelCols, colTime)
    true

// ==================== Build a fresh group at each new period ==================
if newP and hasStats
    g = f_newGroup()
    if showO
        f_add(g, mkLine(startTime, curO, colO, line.style_solid, lnWidth), colO)
        if lblMode != "None"
            f_addLbl(g, mkLabel(startTime, curO, f_lblTxt(2, "", curO), colO), colO)
    // Drawn top of the map to the bottom: +D, +M, open, -M, -D.
    if showD
        f_drawSet(g, startTime, lvlPDm, lvlPDd, lvlPDp, f_bandHi(med2, e1.s2, true), f_bandLo(med2, e1.s2, true), colD, 0)
    if showM
        f_drawSet(g, startTime, lvlPMm, lvlPMd, lvlPMp, f_bandHi(med0, e1.s0, true), f_bandLo(med0, e1.s0, true), colM, 1)
        f_drawSet(g, startTime, lvlNMm, lvlNMd, lvlNMp, f_bandHi(med1, e1.s1, false), f_bandLo(med1, e1.s1, false), colM, 3)
    if showD
        f_drawSet(g, startTime, lvlNDm, lvlNDd, lvlNDp, f_bandHi(med3, e1.s3, false), f_bandLo(med3, e1.s3, false), colD, 4)
    // Phase timing, from the same walk-forward accumulators the table reports.
    f_timeMark(g, startTime, mFrN > 0 ? sumMFr / mFrN : float(na), lvlPMd, lvlNMd, "M")
    f_timeMark(g, startTime, extN > 0 ? sumHiFr / extN : float(na), lvlPDd, lvlNDd, "H")
    f_timeMark(g, startTime, extN > 0 ? sumLoFr / extN : float(na), lvlPDd, lvlNDd, "L")

    if histDim
        f_dim(active)
    array.push(groups, g)
    active := g
    if array.size(groups) > periodsShow
        old = array.shift(groups)
        for fl in old.fills
            linefill.delete(fl)
        for ln in old.lines
            line.delete(ln)
        for lb in old.labels
            label.delete(lb)
        for bx in old.boxes
            box.delete(bx)

if not na(active)
    // "Period end" runs to the projected close of the period, or to the current
    // bar once the period has overrun it. All of this is in milliseconds.
    int periodEnd = startTime + int(periodMs)
    rightX = extendTo == "Last bar" ? time :
         extendTo == "Fixed bars" ? time + extBars * barMs :
         periodEnd > time ? periodEnd : time
    for ln in active.lines
        // level lines are horizontal; the vertical timing markers keep their x
        if line.get_y1(ln) == line.get_y2(ln)
            line.set_x2(ln, rightX)
    if array.size(active.labels) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(active.labels) - 1
            if array.get(active.labelCols, i) != colTime
                label.set_x(array.get(active.labels, i), rightX)
    for bx in active.boxes
        box.set_right(bx, rightX)

// ======================= Sequencing & timing (chart TF) =======================
// Intra-period ordering is invisible on higher-timeframe bars, so this is
// measured on the chart's own bars and carries its own smaller sample.
var int   pBars   = 0
var int   hiBar   = 0
var int   loBar   = 0
var float pHi     = na
var float pLo     = na
var bool  tagM    = false
var bool  tagD    = false
var int   firstM  = -1
var int   firstD  = -1
var float lockPM  = na
var float lockNM  = na
var float lockPD  = na
var float lockND  = na

if newP
    if pBars > 1 and not na(pHi)
        float span = math.max(1.0, float(pBars - 1))
        sumHiFr += float(hiBar) / span
        sumLoFr += float(loBar) / span
        extN += 1.0
        if firstM >= 0 or firstD >= 0
            seqN += 1.0
            if firstM >= 0 and (firstD < 0 or firstM < firstD)
                seqMwin += 1.0
            else if firstD >= 0
                seqDwin += 1.0
        if firstM >= 0
            sumMFr += float(firstM) / span
            mFrN += 1.0
    pBars := 0
    hiBar := 0
    loBar := 0
    pHi := high
    pLo := low
    tagM := false
    tagD := false
    firstM := -1
    firstD := -1
    lockPM := lvlPMd
    lockNM := lvlNMd
    lockPD := lvlPDd
    lockND := lvlNDd
else
    pBars += 1
    if na(pHi) or high > pHi
        pHi := high
        hiBar := pBars
    if na(pLo) or low < pLo
        pLo := low
        loBar := pBars

hitPMnow = not na(lockPM) and high >= lockPM
hitNMnow = not na(lockNM) and low <= lockNM
hitPDnow = not na(lockPD) and high >= lockPD
hitNDnow = not na(lockND) and low <= lockND

newTagM = (hitPMnow or hitNMnow) and not tagM
newTagD = (hitPDnow or hitNDnow) and not tagD
if newTagM
    tagM := true
    firstM := pBars
if newTagD
    tagD := true
    firstD := pBars

// A manipulation is only "confirmed" once price closes back through the level
// it swept — the reversal, not the touch, is the signal.
confM = tagM and ((hitPMnow and close < lockPM) or (hitNMnow and close > lockNM))

// ================================== Alerts ====================================
alertcondition(newTagM, "Manipulation level tagged", "Price reached a manipulation level")
alertcondition(newTagD, "Distribution level tagged", "Price reached a distribution target")
alertcondition(confM,   "Manipulation confirmed",    "Price swept a manipulation level and closed back through")

if alertOn
    if newTagM
        alert("Manipulation level tagged on " + syminfo.ticker + " (" + tfSel + " projection)", alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if newTagD
        alert("Distribution target tagged on " + syminfo.ticker + " (" + tfSel + " projection)", alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if confM
        alert("Manipulation CONFIRMED on " + syminfo.ticker + " — swept and closed back through", alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ================================ Confluence ==================================
// Where levels from different timeframes stack up is where reactions cluster.
var array<box> cfBoxes = array.new<box>()

f_lvlsOf(Res s, float atrp, float o) =>
    array<float> a = array.new<float>()
    float ap = transform == "Log + ATR" ? atrp : na
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.d0, o, ap, true))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.p0, o, ap, true))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.d1, o, ap, false))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.p1, o, ap, false))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.d2, o, ap, true))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.p2, o, ap, true))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.d3, o, ap, false))
    array.push(a, f_lvl(transform, s.p3, o, ap, false))
    a

if barstate.islast and (cf2On or cf3On)
    for bx in cfBoxes
        box.delete(bx)
    array.clear(cfBoxes)
    array<float> base = f_lvlsOf(e1, chartAtrP, curO)
    array<float> other = array.new<float>()
    if cf2On
        array<float> b2 = f_lvlsOf(eB, chartAtrB, curO)
        for v in b2
            array.push(other, v)
    if cf3On
        array<float> b3 = f_lvlsOf(eC, chartAtrC, curO)
        for v in b3
            array.push(other, v)
    int x1 = math.max(0, bar_index - cfBars)
    for a in base
        if not na(a)
            for b in other
                if not na(b) and math.abs(a - b) / a * 100.0 <= cfTol
                    float lo = math.min(a, b)
                    float hi = math.max(a, b)
                    float pad = a * cfTol / 100.0 * 0.5
                    array.push(cfBoxes, box.new(x1, hi + pad, bar_index + cfBars, lo - pad,
                         border_color=color.new(color.yellow, 60), bgcolor=cfCol, xloc=xloc.bar_index))
                    break

// ================================ Stats table =================================
// Laid out top of the map to the bottom (+DIS, +MAN, OPEN, -MAN, -DIS) so the
// rows read in the same order the levels sit on the chart, with the projected
// price alongside each statistic.
f_tablePos(string p) =>
    switch p
        "bottom_left"  => position.bottom_left
        "bottom_right" => position.bottom_right
        "top_center"   => position.top_center
        "top_left"     => position.top_left
        "top_right"    => position.top_right
        "middle_left"  => position.middle_left
        "middle_right" => position.middle_right
        => position.bottom_center

posSel  = f_tablePos(tblPos)
sizeSel = tblSize == "auto" ? size.auto : tblSize == "small" ? size.small : tblSize == "normal" ? size.normal : size.tiny

// Units follow the measure: ATR mode is dimensionless, the rest are percentages.
f_ratio(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "—" : transform == "Log + ATR" ? str.tostring(v, "#.##") + "x" : str.tostring(v * 100, "#.##") + "%"

f_ratioSe(float v, float se) =>
    na(v) ? "—" : f_ratio(v) + (na(se) ? "" : " ±" + (transform == "Log + ATR" ? str.tostring(se, "#.##") : str.tostring(se * 100, "#.##")))

f_rate(float r) => na(r) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(r * 100)) + "%"

f_price(float p) => na(p) ? "—" : str.tostring(p, format.mintick)

var table t = table.new(posSel, 8, 12, border_width=1,
     border_color=color.new(color.gray, 60), frame_width=1, frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 60))

// A thin sample dims its rows rather than flooding them, so the table stays
// readable while still saying plainly that the numbers are not yet evidence.
txtC  = thin ? color.new(tblTxtCol, 55) : tblTxtCol
dimC  = color.new(tblTxtCol, 45)
warnC = color.new(color.orange, 0)

// One level row: tag, projected price, then the statistics behind it.
f_lvlRow(int r, int li, float px, float mn, float md, float pc, float se, float nn,
         float rr, float hh, float rrp, float hhp, color tagCol) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, r, f_levelTag(li), text_color=thin ? color.new(tagCol, 55) : tagCol,
         text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 1, r, f_price(px), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 2, r, f_ratioSe(mn, se), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 3, r, f_ratio(md), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 4, r, f_ratio(pc), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 5, r, f_rate(rr), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol,
         tooltip="percentile level reach: " + f_rate(rrp))
    table.cell(t, 6, r, f_rate(hh), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol,
         tooltip="percentile level hold: " + f_rate(hhp))
    table.cell(t, 7, r, str.tostring(nn, "#"), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)

if barstate.islast and showTbl
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, tfSel, text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Measure: " + transform + (uncondMode ? " · unconditional" : " · conditional") + (recOn ? " · half-life " + str.tostring(halfLife) : "") + (condMode != "None" ? " · conditioned on " + condMode : ""))
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, "Price",    text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="The median level, which is the line the reach and hold columns are measured against.")
    table.cell(t, 2, 0, "Mean ±SE", text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 3, 0, "Median",   text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 4, 0, "Pctile",   text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 5, 0, "Reach",    text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="How often price TOUCHED the median level. This is the number you want for setting targets.")
    table.cell(t, 6, 0, "Hold",     text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Of the times it was reached, how often price closed back through it — the reversal rate.")
    table.cell(t, 7, 0, "n",        text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)

    // Levels, top of the map to the bottom.
    f_lvlRow(1, 0, lvlPDd, mean2, med2, pct2, se2, n2, e1.rd2, e1.hd2, e1.rp2, e1.hp2, colD)
    f_lvlRow(2, 1, lvlPMd, mean0, med0, pct0, se0, n0, e1.rd0, e1.hd0, e1.rp0, e1.hp0, colM)

    // Open
    table.cell(t, 0, 3, f_levelTag(2), text_color=colO, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 1, 3, f_price(curO), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    for c = 2 to 7
        table.cell(t, c, 3, "", bgcolor=tblBgCol)

    f_lvlRow(4, 3, lvlNMd, mean1, med1, pct1, se1, n1, e1.rd1, e1.hd1, e1.rp1, e1.hp1, colM)
    f_lvlRow(5, 4, lvlNDd, mean3, med3, pct3, se3, n3, e1.rd3, e1.hd3, e1.rp3, e1.hp3, colD)

    // Typical candle range implied by the median levels: the up-close case runs
    // from the lower manipulation to the upper distribution, the down-close case
    // from the upper manipulation to the lower distribution.
    if showRange
        float rngUp = na(lvlPDd) or na(lvlNMd) ? float(na) : lvlPDd - lvlNMd
        float rngDn = na(lvlPMd) or na(lvlNDd) ? float(na) : lvlPMd - lvlNDd
        float rng   = na(rngUp) or na(rngDn) ? float(na) : (rngUp + rngDn) / 2.0
        table.cell(t, 0, 6, "RNG", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Average of the up-close range (+MAN to +DIS) and the down-close range (-MAN to -DIS), both taken from the median levels.")
        table.cell(t, 1, 6, f_price(rng), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        for c = 2 to 7
            table.cell(t, c, 6, "", bgcolor=tblBgCol)

    // Whipsaw / volatility
    table.cell(t, 0, 7, "both-side", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="How often BOTH manipulation levels were tagged in the same period — the whipsaw rate, i.e. how often this model's premise fails.")
    table.cell(t, 1, 7, f_rate(e1.bothR), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 2, 7, "vol", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 3, 7, na(chartAtrP) ? "—" : str.tostring(chartAtrP * 100, "#.##") + "%", text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Current ATR as a percentage of price on the projection timeframe. In 'Log + ATR' mode this is the scale every stored ratio is multiplied by.")
    table.cell(t, 4, 7, "scored", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 5, 7, str.tostring(e1.evalN, "#"), text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Periods scored walk-forward for the reach/hold columns, over the same rolling window as the ratios.")
    for c = 6 to 7
        table.cell(t, c, 7, "", bgcolor=tblBgCol)

    // Source / sample health
    nFeeds = 1 + (use2 ? 1 : 0) + (use3 ? 1 : 0)
    srcTip = statSym1 + (use2 ? "\n" + sym2 : "") + (use3 ? "\n" + sym3 : "")
    table.cell(t, 0, 8, "Source", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
    table.cell(t, 1, 8, useCustomFeed ? statSym1 : "Chart", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip=srcTip)
    table.cell(t, 2, 8, nFeeds > 1 ? "+" + str.tostring(nFeeds - 1) + " pooled" : "", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip=srcTip)
    table.cell(t, 3, 8, tfInverted ? "CHART > PROJ TF" : thin ? "THIN SAMPLE" : "", text_color=(tfInverted or thin) ? warnC : dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip=tfInverted ? "Your chart timeframe is coarser than the projection timeframe, so every chart bar registers as a new period and the levels are meaningless. Raise the projection timeframe above your chart timeframe." : thin ? "At least one level has fewer than " + str.tostring(minSample) + " samples. Treat these levels as indicative only." : "")
    for c = 4 to 7
        table.cell(t, c, 8, "", bgcolor=tblBgCol)

    if showSeq
        table.cell(t, 0, 9, "Sequence", text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Measured on the chart timeframe over " + str.tostring(seqN, "#") + " periods — a much smaller sample than the level statistics above.")
        table.cell(t, 1, 9, "M first", text_color=colM, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 2, 9, seqN > 0 ? f_rate(seqMwin / seqN) : "—", text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 3, 9, "D first", text_color=colD, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 4, 9, seqN > 0 ? f_rate(seqDwin / seqN) : "—", text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 5, 9, "n=" + str.tostring(seqN, "#"), text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        for c = 6 to 7
            table.cell(t, c, 9, "", bgcolor=tblBgCol)

        table.cell(t, 0, 10, "Timing", text_color=tblTxtCol, text_size=sizeSel, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=tblBgCol, tooltip="Average position within the period, as a fraction of its length, at which each event printed. These are the fractions the chart's vertical phase markers are drawn from.")
        table.cell(t, 1, 10, "high at", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 2, 10, extN > 0 ? str.tostring(sumHiFr / extN * 100, "#") + "%" : "—", text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 3, 10, "low at", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 4, 10, extN > 0 ? str.tostring(sumLoFr / extN * 100, "#") + "%" : "—", text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 5, 10, "M tag at", text_color=dimC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 6, 10, mFrN > 0 ? str.tostring(sumMFr / mFrN * 100, "#") + "%" : "—", text_color=txtC, text_size=sizeSel, bgcolor=tblBgCol)
        table.cell(t, 7, 10, "", bgcolor=tblBgCol)


// #############################################################################
// ##  PART 2 OF 2 - EXPANSION MODEL [Pro+]                                   ##
// #############################################################################

//#region [INPUTS]

grpModel   = 'General Settings'
showAlerts = input.bool(true, 'Alerts?', group = grpModel, inline = 'alerts', tooltip = "To turn on the alerts, follow these steps:\n\n1) Make sure that the 'Alerts?' toggle is ON.\n2) Find, and click on, the three dots next to the indicator title on the top left of your chart, or right-click on the indicator on the chart.\n3) Click 'Add Alert on Fractal Model [Pro+]'\n4) Choose the Alert Name, if you wish, and confirm by clicking 'Create'")
showEarlyCisdAlerts = input.bool(false, 'Early CISD Alerts?', group = grpModel, inline = 'alerts', tooltip = "The global 'Alerts?' toggle above acts as a master switch. If it is OFF, Early CISD alerts will not fire even if this toggle is ON.")
showHistory = input.int(1, 'History', minval = 0, maxval = 40, group = grpModel, tooltip = 'Number of past setups (valid or invalidated) to keep drawn on the chart. 0 = unlimited.')
biasFilter = input.string('Neutral', 'Bias', options = ['Neutral', 'Bullish', 'Bearish'], group = grpModel)
modelType  = input.string('Auto', 'Fractal', options = ['Custom', 'Auto', '1m-15m', '3m-30m', '5m-1H', '15m-4H', '1H-1D', '4H-1W', '1D-1W'], group = grpModel, inline = 'fractal')
showEarlyCisd = input.bool(true, 'Early CISD', group = grpModel, inline = 'fractal')
showEarlyC2 = input.bool(true, 'Early C2 Sweep', group = grpModel, inline = 'earlyc2', tooltip = "Marks C2 the moment the forming HTF candle takes out the previous HTF candle's low (bullish) or high (bearish), instead of waiting for that candle to close and the next one to open.\n\nThe early marker tracks the running sweep extreme while the candle is still forming. When the HTF candle closes it is replaced by the confirmed C2 setup (if it closed back inside C1's range) or removed (if it did not).")
showEarlyC2Alerts = input.bool(false, 'Alerts?', group = grpModel, inline = 'earlyc2', tooltip = "The global 'Alerts?' toggle acts as a master switch. If it is OFF, Early C2 Sweep alerts will not fire even if this toggle is ON.")
customLTF  = input.timeframe('5',  'Custom LTF                      ', group = grpModel, inline = 'custom', active = modelType == 'Custom')
customHTF  = input.timeframe('60', '', group = grpModel, inline = 'custom', tooltip = 'Only active when Alignment is set to Custom', active = modelType == 'Custom')

grpCandles     = 'HTF Candles'
htfCandleCount = input.int(4, 'HTF Candles', minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = grpCandles, inline = 'count')
hideHtf        = input.bool(false, 'Hide?', group = grpCandles, inline = 'count', tooltip = 'Hide HTF candles preview')
candleOffsetIn = input.int(0, 'Offset', minval = 0, group = grpCandles)

bullBody   = input.color(color.new(color.green, 0), 'Body', group = grpCandles, inline = 'body')
bearBody   = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', group = grpCandles, inline = 'body')
borderBull = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), 'Borders', group = grpCandles, inline = 'border')
borderBear = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', group = grpCandles, inline = 'border')
wickBull   = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), 'Wick', group = grpCandles, inline = 'wick')
wickBear   = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', group = grpCandles, inline = 'wick')

showHtfOpen  = input.bool(true, 'HTF Open', group = grpCandles, inline = 'htfopen')
htfOpenColor = input.color(color.new(#1a1a1a, 30), '', group = grpCandles, inline = 'htfopen')
htfOpenStyle = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpCandles, inline = 'htfopen')
htfOpenWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpCandles, inline = 'htfopen')

showVlines = input.bool(true, 'O/C Time', group = grpCandles, inline = 'vline')
lineColor  = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 60), '', group = grpCandles, inline = 'vline')
lineStyle  = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpCandles, inline = 'vline')
lineWidth  = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpCandles, inline = 'vline')

showLH  = input.bool(false, 'L/H Lines', group = grpCandles, inline = 'lh')
lhColor = input.color(color.new(#1a1a1a, 30), '', group = grpCandles, inline = 'lh')
lhStyle = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpCandles, inline = 'lh')
lhWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpCandles, inline = 'lh')

grpVisuals = 'Model Style'
showLabels = input.bool(true, 'Labels?', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'lbl')
labelSize  = input.string('Small', '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'lbl', options = ['Tiny', 'Small', 'Normal', 'Large', 'Huge'], active = showLabels)
showSweep  = input.bool(false, 'Candle 1 Sweep', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'sweep')
sweepColor = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'sweep')
sweepStyle = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpVisuals, inline = 'sweep')
sweepWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpVisuals, inline = 'sweep')

earlyC2Color = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 0), 'Early C2 Sweep', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'earlyc2line', active = showEarlyC2)
earlyC2Style = input.string('Dotted', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpVisuals, inline = 'earlyc2line', active = showEarlyC2)
earlyC2Width = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpVisuals, inline = 'earlyc2line', active = showEarlyC2)

earlyCisdColor = input.color(color.new(color.blue, 0), 'Early CISD', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'earlycisd', active = showEarlyCisd)
earlyCisdStyle = input.string('Dashed', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpVisuals, inline = 'earlycisd', active = showEarlyCisd)
earlyCisdWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpVisuals, inline = 'earlycisd', active = showEarlyCisd)

showBullCisd  = input.bool(true, 'Bullish CISD', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bullcisd')
cisdBullColor = input.color(color.new(color.blue, 0), '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bullcisd')
cisdBullStyle = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bullcisd', active = showBullCisd)
cisdBullWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bullcisd', active = showBullCisd)

showBearCisd  = input.bool(true, 'Bearish CISD', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bearcisd')
cisdBearColor = input.color(color.new(color.blue, 0), '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bearcisd')
cisdBearStyle = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bearcisd', active = showBearCisd)
cisdBearWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpVisuals, inline = 'bearcisd', active = showBearCisd)

showEQ  = input.bool(true, 'Candle Equilibrium', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'eq')
eqColor = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'eq')
eqStyle = input.string('Dotted', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpVisuals, inline = 'eq')
eqWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpVisuals, inline = 'eq')

showTSpot      = input.bool(true, 'T-Spot Box', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'tspot')
tSpotBullColor = input.color(color.new(color.green, 80), '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'tspot')
tSpotBearColor = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 80), '', group = grpVisuals, inline = 'tspot')

grpStdDev   = 'Deviations'
showStdDev  = input.bool(false, 'Enable Projections?', group = grpStdDev, inline = 'stdb')
stdDevInput = input.string('-1,-2,-3', '', group = grpStdDev, inline = 'stdb', active = showStdDev)
stdDevCalc  = input.string('Wick', 'Method', options = ['Wick', 'Body'], group = grpStdDev, inline = 'stdb', active = showStdDev)
stdDevColor = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', group = grpStdDev, inline = 'stdc', active = showStdDev)
stdDevStyle = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = grpStdDev, inline = 'stdc', active = showStdDev)
stdDevWidth = input.int(1, '', minval = 1, group = grpStdDev, inline = 'stdc', active = showStdDev)
stdDevLabelGap = input.int(4, 'Label Gap', minval = 0, maxval = 50, group = grpStdDev, tooltip = 'Bars of clearance between the HTF candle preview and the projection price labels.', active = showStdDev)

grpDash  = 'Dashboard'
boolTable = input.bool(true, 'Show Dashboard', group = grpDash)
tableVert = input.string('Top', '', options = ['Top', 'Middle', 'Bottom'], inline = 'loc', group = grpDash)
tableHorz = input.string('Right', '', options = ['Left', 'Center', 'Right'], inline = 'loc', group = grpDash)
dashTextColor = input.color(color.new(#131722, 0), 'Text', group = grpDash, inline = 'color')
dashBgColor   = input.color(color.new(#ffffff, 0), 'Background', group = grpDash, inline = 'color')

//#endregion

//#region [CONSTANTS AND STATE]

candleSpacing = 3
noColor       = color.new(#000000, 100)

type HtfCandle
    float o
    float h
    float l
    float c
    int   hBar
    int   lBar
    box   body
    line  wickUp
    line  wickDown
    line  eqLine
    int   midX
    line  sweepLine   = na
    bool  triggerBuy  = false
    bool  triggerSell = false

type PeriodState
    float prevHigh        = na
    float prevLow         = na
    int   prevHighBar     = na
    int   prevLowBar      = na
    float prevPrevHigh    = na
    float prevPrevLow     = na
    int   prevPrevHighBar = na
    int   prevPrevLowBar  = na
    bool  prevC2Buy       = false
    bool  prevC2Sell      = false

type StdDevData
    array<line>  lines
    array<label> labels

type C2Setup
    bool  isBull
    float extreme
    int   phase     = 1
    bool  dead      = false
    label c2Lbl
    box   c3Box     = na
    line  c3Dash    = na
    float cisdLevel     = na
    int   cisdIndex     = na
    bool  cisdConfirmed = false
    line  cisdLine      = na
    label cisdLabel     = na
    StdDevData stdDevData = na
    box   c4Box     = na
    line  c4Dash    = na
    label c4Lbl     = na
    float c4Top     = na
    float c4Bottom  = na
    bool  c4Invalid = false

type SetupRecord
    C2Setup setup
    int     creationBar

type EarlyCisdRecord
    line  ln
    label lbl
    int   barIndex

// Provisional C2 marker for the HTF candle that is still forming.
type EarlySweep
    bool  isBull
    float extreme
    int   extremeBar
    label lbl
    line  ln

var array<HtfCandle>        htfCandles           = array.new<HtfCandle>()
var array<line>             vLines               = array.new<line>()
var array<line>             hLines               = array.new<line>()
var array<line>             lLines               = array.new<line>()
var PeriodState              state                = PeriodState.new()
var C2Setup                  buySetup             = na
var C2Setup                  sellSetup            = na
var array<SetupRecord>       setupRecords         = array.new<SetupRecord>()
var array<EarlyCisdRecord>   bullEarlyCisdRecords = array.new<EarlyCisdRecord>()
var array<EarlyCisdRecord>   bearEarlyCisdRecords = array.new<EarlyCisdRecord>()
var EarlySweep               bullEarlySweep       = na
var EarlySweep               bearEarlySweep       = na
var int                      htfOpenBar           = na
var line                     htfOpenLn            = na

allowBuy  = biasFilter != 'Bearish'
allowSell = biasFilter != 'Bullish'

//#endregion

//#region [FUNCTIONS]

tfLabel(string tfStr) =>
    switch tfStr
        '1'   => '1m'
        '3'   => '3m'
        '5'   => '5m'
        '15'  => '15m'
        '60'  => '1h'
        '240' => '4h'
        '1D'  => '1D'
        'D'   => '1D'
        '1W'  => '1W'
        'W'   => '1W'
        '1M'  => '1M'
        'M'   => '1M'
        =>       tfStr + 'm'

tfMins(string tfStr) =>
    switch tfStr
        '1D' => 1440
        'D'  => 1440
        '1W' => 10080
        'W'  => 10080
        '1M' => 43200
        'M'  => 43200
        =>      int(str.tonumber(tfStr))

curTfCode() =>
    timeframe.isdaily ? '1D' : timeframe.isweekly ? '1W' : timeframe.ismonthly ? '1M' : timeframe.period

tablePosition(string vert, string horz) =>
    switch vert + '-' + horz
        'Top-Left'      => position.top_left
        'Top-Center'    => position.top_center
        'Top-Right'     => position.top_right
        'Middle-Left'   => position.middle_left
        'Middle-Center' => position.middle_center
        'Middle-Right'  => position.middle_right
        'Bottom-Left'   => position.bottom_left
        'Bottom-Center' => position.bottom_center
        'Bottom-Right'  => position.bottom_right
        =>                 position.top_right

lineStyleFromStr(string s) =>
    switch s
        'Solid'  => line.style_solid
        'Dashed' => line.style_dashed
        'Dotted' => line.style_dotted
        =>          line.style_dashed

textSize(string s) =>
    switch s
        'Tiny'   => size.tiny
        'Small'  => size.small
        'Normal' => size.normal
        'Large'  => size.large
        =>          size.huge

directionalLabel(int xBar, float yPrice, string txt, bool bullish) =>
    label.new(xBar, yPrice, text = txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = bullish ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = na, textcolor = color.gray, size = textSize(labelSize), text_font_family = font.family_monospace)

eqLineColor() => showEQ ? eqColor : noColor

drawSweepLine(int fromBar, float fromPrice, int toBar) =>
    line ln = showSweep ? line.new(fromBar, fromPrice, toBar, fromPrice, color = sweepColor, style = lineStyleFromStr(sweepStyle), width = sweepWidth) : na
    ln

newLHLine(float price) =>
    line.new(bar_index, price, bar_index, price, xloc.bar_index, extend.none, lhColor, lineStyleFromStr(lhStyle), lhWidth)

updateLHLine(line ln, float price) =>
    line.set_xy1(ln, line.get_x1(ln), price)
    line.set_xy2(ln, bar_index, price)
    line.set_color(ln, lhColor)
    line.set_style(ln, lineStyleFromStr(lhStyle))
    line.set_width(ln, lhWidth)

autoHTF() =>
    switch timeframe.period
        '1'   => '15'
        '3'   => '30'
        '5'   => '60'
        '15'  => '240'
        '60'  => '1D'
        '240' => '1W'
        '1D'  => '1M'
        =>       '1M'

ltfCode() =>
    switch modelType
        '1m-15m' => '1'
        '3m-30m' => '3'
        '5m-1H'  => '5'
        '15m-4H' => '15'
        '1H-1D'  => '60'
        '4H-1W'  => '240'
        '1D-1W'  => '1D'
        'Custom' => customLTF
        =>          curTfCode()

isAutoValidTf(int mins) => mins == 1 or mins == 3 or mins == 5 or mins == 15 or mins == 60 or mins == 240 or mins == 1440

method delete(HtfCandle c) =>
    box.delete(c.body)
    line.delete(c.wickUp)
    line.delete(c.wickDown)
    line.delete(c.eqLine)
    line.delete(c.sweepLine)

method update(HtfCandle c, float curH, float curL, float curC, int curBar) =>
    if curH > c.h
        c.h    := curH
        c.hBar := curBar
    if curL < c.l
        c.l    := curL
        c.lBar := curBar
    c.c := curC
    c

method draw(HtfCandle c, int leftBar) =>
    bool  isBull = c.c >= c.o
    int   midX   = leftBar + 1
    float eq     = (c.h + c.l) / 2
    box.set_left(c.body, leftBar)
    box.set_right(c.body, leftBar + 2)
    box.set_top(c.body, math.max(c.o, c.c))
    box.set_bottom(c.body, math.min(c.o, c.c))
    box.set_bgcolor(c.body, isBull ? bullBody : bearBody)
    box.set_border_color(c.body, isBull ? borderBull : borderBear)
    line.set_x1(c.wickUp, midX)
    line.set_x2(c.wickUp, midX)
    line.set_y1(c.wickUp, c.h)
    line.set_y2(c.wickUp, math.max(c.o, c.c))
    line.set_color(c.wickUp, isBull ? wickBull : wickBear)
    line.set_x1(c.wickDown, midX)
    line.set_x2(c.wickDown, midX)
    line.set_y1(c.wickDown, c.l)
    line.set_y2(c.wickDown, math.min(c.o, c.c))
    line.set_color(c.wickDown, isBull ? wickBull : wickBear)
    line.set_x1(c.eqLine, midX)
    line.set_x2(c.eqLine, midX)
    line.set_y1(c.eqLine, eq)
    line.set_y2(c.eqLine, eq)
    line.set_color(c.eqLine, eqLineColor())
    line.set_style(c.eqLine, lineStyleFromStr(eqStyle))
    line.set_width(c.eqLine, eqWidth)
    c.midX := midX

newHtfCandle() =>
    HtfCandle.new(open, high, low, close, bar_index, bar_index,
         box.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, low, border_color = borderBull, border_width = 1),
         line.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, high, color = wickBull),
         line.new(bar_index, low, bar_index, low, color = wickBull),
         line.new(bar_index, high, bar_index, high, color = noColor),
         na)

drawEarlyCisd(bool isBull, float level, int idx, int confirmBar) =>
    array<EarlyCisdRecord> target = isBull ? bullEarlyCisdRecords : bearEarlyCisdRecords
    if showEarlyCisd
        ln = line.new(idx, level, confirmBar + 3, level, color = earlyCisdColor, style = lineStyleFromStr(earlyCisdStyle), width = earlyCisdWidth)
        label lbl = na
        if showLabels
            lbl := label.new(confirmBar + 3, level, isBull ? '+CISD' : '-CISD', xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = na, textcolor = earlyCisdColor, size = textSize(labelSize), text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
        target.push(EarlyCisdRecord.new(ln, lbl, confirmBar))
    if showAlerts and showEarlyCisdAlerts
        alert((isBull ? 'Bullish' : 'Bearish') + ' Early CISD confirmed on ' + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

pruneEarlyCisd(array<EarlyCisdRecord> recs, int thresholdBar) =>
    if not na(thresholdBar)
        while recs.size() > 0 and recs.first().barIndex < thresholdBar
            evicted = recs.shift()
            line.delete(evicted.ln)
            if not na(evicted.lbl)
                label.delete(evicted.lbl)

consumeLastEarlyCisd(array<EarlyCisdRecord> recs) =>
    if recs.size() > 0
        evicted = recs.pop()
        line.delete(evicted.ln)
        if not na(evicted.lbl)
            label.delete(evicted.lbl)

parseFloats(string src) =>
    var out = array.new<float>()
    array.clear(out)
    for part in str.split(str.replace_all(src, ' ', ''), ',')
        v = str.tonumber(part)
        if not na(v)
            out.push(v)
    out

createStdDevProjections(C2Setup s, int confirmBar) =>
    if showStdDev
        devs = parseFloats(stdDevInput)
        if devs.size() > 0
            off     = bar_index - s.cisdIndex
            useWick = stdDevCalc == 'Wick'

            level0 = s.cisdLevel
            level1 = s.extreme
            if not useWick
                for j = 0 to 50
                    if s.isBull ? low[j] == s.extreme : high[j] == s.extreme
                        level1 := s.isBull ? math.min(open[j], close[j]) : math.max(open[j], close[j])
                        break

            leftBar = s.cisdIndex
            if s.cisdIndex < bar_index
                prevBetter = s.isBull
                     ? (useWick ? high[off + 1] > high[off] : math.max(open[off + 1], close[off + 1]) > math.max(open[off], close[off]))
                     : (useWick ? low[off + 1]  < low[off]  : math.min(open[off + 1], close[off + 1]) < math.min(open[off], close[off]))
                if prevBetter
                    leftBar := s.cisdIndex - 1

            rightBar   = confirmBar + 3
            priceRange = s.isBull ? level0 - level1 : level1 - level0
            lns        = array.new<line>()
            lbs        = array.new<label>()

            for dev in devs
                devPrice = s.isBull ? level0 - priceRange * dev : level0 + priceRange * dev
                lns.push(line.new(leftBar, devPrice, rightBar, devPrice, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = stdDevColor, width = stdDevWidth, style = lineStyleFromStr(stdDevStyle)))
                if showLabels
                    lbs.push(label.new(rightBar, devPrice, str.tostring(dev) + '  ' + str.tostring(devPrice, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = na, textcolor = stdDevColor, size = textSize(labelSize), text_font_family = font.family_monospace))

            s.stdDevData := StdDevData.new(lns, lbs)

confirmCisd(C2Setup s, int confirmBar) =>
    s.cisdConfirmed := true
    showLine = s.isBull ? showBullCisd : showBearCisd
    clr      = s.isBull ? cisdBullColor : cisdBearColor
    lnStyle  = s.isBull ? cisdBullStyle : cisdBearStyle
    lnWidth  = s.isBull ? cisdBullWidth : cisdBearWidth
    if showLine
        s.cisdLine := line.new(s.cisdIndex, s.cisdLevel, confirmBar + 3, s.cisdLevel, color = clr, style = lineStyleFromStr(lnStyle), width = lnWidth)
        if showLabels
            s.cisdLabel := label.new(confirmBar + 3, s.cisdLevel, s.isBull ? '+CISD' : '-CISD', xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = na, textcolor = clr, size = textSize(labelSize), text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
    createStdDevProjections(s, confirmBar)

deleteSetupVisuals(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s)
        if not na(s.c2Lbl)
            label.delete(s.c2Lbl)
        if not na(s.cisdLine)
            line.delete(s.cisdLine)
        if not na(s.cisdLabel)
            label.delete(s.cisdLabel)
        if not na(s.c3Box)
            box.delete(s.c3Box)
        if not na(s.c3Dash)
            line.delete(s.c3Dash)
        if not na(s.c4Box)
            box.delete(s.c4Box)
        if not na(s.c4Dash)
            line.delete(s.c4Dash)
        if not na(s.c4Lbl)
            label.delete(s.c4Lbl)
        if not na(s.stdDevData)
            if not na(s.stdDevData.lines)
                for ln in s.stdDevData.lines
                    line.delete(ln)
            if not na(s.stdDevData.labels)
                for lb in s.stdDevData.labels
                    label.delete(lb)

registerRecord(C2Setup s) =>
    setupRecords.push(SetupRecord.new(s, bar_index))
    while showHistory > 0 and setupRecords.size() > showHistory
        evicted = setupRecords.shift()
        deleteSetupVisuals(evicted.setup)
    earliestVisibleBar = setupRecords.size() > 0 ? setupRecords.first().creationBar : na
    pruneEarlyCisd(bullEarlyCisdRecords, earliestVisibleBar)
    pruneEarlyCisd(bearEarlyCisdRecords, earliestVisibleBar)

autoTf = switch modelType
    '1m-15m' => '15'
    '3m-30m' => '30'
    '5m-1H'  => '60'
    '15m-4H' => '240'
    '1H-1D'  => '1D'
    '4H-1W'  => '1W'
    '1D-1W'  => '1W'
    'Custom' => customHTF
    =>          autoHTF()

validTf = modelType == 'Auto' ? isAutoValidTf(tfMins(curTfCode())) : tfMins(curTfCode()) <= tfMins(ltfCode())

[currentO, currentH, currentL, currentC, prevH1, prevL1] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, autoTf, [open[0], high[0], low[0], close[0], high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

c2Buy         = currentL < prevL1 and currentC > prevL1
c2Sell        = currentH > prevH1 and currentC < prevH1
periodChanged = time(autoTf) != time(autoTf)[1]

drawPhase(bool isBull, bool isC4) =>
    mid   = (state.prevHigh + state.prevLow) / 2
    top   = math.max(open, mid)
    bot   = math.min(open, mid)
    yDash = isBull ? bot : top
    bxCol = isBull ? tSpotBullColor : tSpotBearColor
    box   bx   = showTSpot ? box.new(bar_index, top, bar_index, bot, border_color = na, bgcolor = bxCol) : na
    line  dash = showEQ ? line.new(bar_index, yDash, bar_index, yDash, color = eqColor, width = eqWidth, style = lineStyleFromStr(eqStyle)) : na
    label lbl  = na
    if isC4 and showTSpot and showLabels and validTf
        lbl := directionalLabel(bar_index + 2, isBull ? bot : top, 'C4', isBull)
    [bx, dash, lbl, top, bot]

// Draws the provisional C2 marker: the swept C1 level plus a label pinned to the
// running extreme of the HTF candle that is still forming.
newEarlySweep(bool isBull, float extremePrice, int extremeBar, float sweptLevel, int sweptBar) =>
    line ln = line.new(sweptBar, sweptLevel, bar_index, sweptLevel, xloc.bar_index, extend.none, earlyC2Color, lineStyleFromStr(earlyC2Style), earlyC2Width)
    label lbl = na
    if showLabels and validTf
        lbl := label.new(extremeBar, extremePrice, text = 'C2', xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = isBull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = na, textcolor = earlyC2Color, size = textSize(labelSize), text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
    EarlySweep.new(isBull, extremePrice, extremeBar, lbl, ln)

method trackExtreme(EarlySweep s, float extremePrice, int extremeBar) =>
    if not na(s)
        line.set_x2(s.ln, bar_index)
        extended = s.isBull ? extremePrice < s.extreme : extremePrice > s.extreme
        if extended
            s.extreme    := extremePrice
            s.extremeBar := extremeBar
            if not na(s.lbl)
                label.set_xy(s.lbl, extremeBar, extremePrice)
    s

clearEarlySweep(EarlySweep s) =>
    if not na(s)
        line.delete(s.ln)
        if not na(s.lbl)
            label.delete(s.lbl)
    EarlySweep cleared = na
    cleared

newSetup(bool isBull, float extreme, label c2Lbl, float cisdLevel, int cisdIndex, bool cisdAlreadyConfirmed, int cisdConfirmBar) =>
    s = C2Setup.new(isBull, extreme, 1, false, c2Lbl)
    [bx, dash, _, _, _] = drawPhase(isBull, false)
    s.c3Box     := bx
    s.c3Dash    := dash
    s.cisdLevel := cisdLevel
    s.cisdIndex := cisdIndex
    if cisdAlreadyConfirmed and not na(cisdLevel) and not na(cisdIndex) and not na(cisdConfirmBar)
        confirmCisd(s, cisdConfirmBar)
    registerRecord(s)
    s

method advanceToC4(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s.c3Box)
        box.set_right(s.c3Box, bar_index)
        line.set_x2(s.c3Dash, bar_index)
    [bx, dash, lbl, top, bot] = drawPhase(s.isBull, true)
    s.c4Box     := bx
    s.c4Dash    := dash
    s.c4Lbl     := lbl
    s.c4Top     := top
    s.c4Bottom  := bot
    s.phase     := 2
    s.c4Invalid := false
    s

method finish(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s.c4Box)
        box.set_right(s.c4Box, bar_index)
        line.set_x2(s.c4Dash, bar_index)
    s.phase := 0
    s

method deleteStdDev(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s.stdDevData)
        if not na(s.stdDevData.lines)
            for ln in s.stdDevData.lines
                line.delete(ln)
        if not na(s.stdDevData.labels)
            for lb in s.stdDevData.labels
                label.delete(lb)
        s.stdDevData := na
    s

method extendAndCheck(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s) and not s.dead and s.phase != 0
        box  extBox  = s.phase == 1 ? s.c3Box : s.c4Box
        line extDash = s.phase == 1 ? s.c3Dash : s.c4Dash
        if not na(extBox)
            box.set_right(extBox, bar_index)
            line.set_x2(extDash, bar_index)

        c2Breach = s.isBull ? low < s.extreme : high > s.extreme
        if c2Breach
            if not na(s.c2Lbl)
                label.set_text(s.c2Lbl, 'XC2')
                label.set_textcolor(s.c2Lbl, s.phase == 2 ? color.orange : color.red)
            if not na(s.c3Box)
                box.delete(s.c3Box)
                s.c3Box := na
            if not na(s.c3Dash)
                line.delete(s.c3Dash)
                s.c3Dash := na
            if not na(s.c4Box)
                box.delete(s.c4Box)
                s.c4Box := na
            if not na(s.c4Dash)
                line.delete(s.c4Dash)
                s.c4Dash := na
            if not na(s.c4Lbl)
                label.delete(s.c4Lbl)
                s.c4Lbl := na
            s.deleteStdDev()
            s.dead  := true
            s.phase := 0
    s

method checkC4Invalid(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s) and not s.dead and s.phase == 2 and not s.c4Invalid
        invalid = s.isBull ? close[1] < s.c4Bottom : close[1] > s.c4Top
        if invalid
            s.c4Invalid := true
            if not na(s.c4Lbl)
                label.set_text(s.c4Lbl, 'XC4')
                label.set_textcolor(s.c4Lbl, color.red)
            if not na(s.c4Dash)
                line.set_color(s.c4Dash, color.red)
            if not na(s.c4Box)
                box.delete(s.c4Box)
                s.c4Box := na
    s

method checkCisdConfirm(C2Setup s) =>
    if not na(s) and not s.dead and not s.cisdConfirmed and s.phase != 0 and not na(s.cisdLevel) and not na(s.cisdIndex)
        confirmed = s.isBull ? close > s.cisdLevel : close < s.cisdLevel
        if confirmed
            confirmCisd(s, bar_index)
    s

processC2(bool trigger, bool allow, bool isBull, float extremePrice, int extremeBar, float sweepFromPrice, int sweepFromBar, float cisdLevel, int cisdIndex, bool cisdAlreadyConfirmed, int cisdConfirmBar, C2Setup existing) =>
    C2Setup result = existing
    if trigger and allow
        label lbl = (validTf and showLabels) ? directionalLabel(extremeBar, extremePrice, 'C2', isBull) : na
        drawSweepLine(sweepFromBar, sweepFromPrice, bar_index)
        result := newSetup(isBull, extremePrice, lbl, cisdLevel, cisdIndex, cisdAlreadyConfirmed, cisdConfirmBar)
    else if periodChanged and not na(existing) and not existing.dead
        result := existing.phase == 1 ? existing.advanceToC4() : existing.phase == 2 ? existing.finish() : existing
    result

markTrigger(bool trigger, bool allow, int idx, bool isBuy) =>
    if trigger and allow and htfCandles.size() > idx
        c = htfCandles.get(idx)
        if isBuy
            c.triggerBuy := true
        else
            c.triggerSell := true

//#endregion

//#region [LOGIC]

var float o0 = open
var float h0 = high
var float l0 = low
var float o1 = open
var float h1 = high
var float l1 = low

var int h0Bar = bar_index
var int l0Bar = bar_index
var int h1Bar = na
var int l1Bar = na

if periodChanged
    o1 := o0[1]
    h1 := h0[1]
    l1 := l0[1]
    h1Bar := h0Bar[1]
    l1Bar := l0Bar[1]
    o0 := open
    h0 := high
    l0 := low
    h0Bar := bar_index
    l0Bar := bar_index

if high >= h0
    h0    := high
    h0Bar := bar_index
if low <= l0
    l0    := low
    l0Bar := bar_index

bool emUp = close > open
bool emDw = close < open
bool emEq = close == open

var float bullLevelFixed = na
var int   bullIndexFixed = na
var float bearLevelFixed = na
var int   bearIndexFixed = na

if low == l0 and low < l1
    if (emDw[0] or emEq[0]) and (emUp[1] or emEq[1]) and not (emEq[0] and emEq[1])
        bullLevelFixed := open
        bullIndexFixed := bar_index
    else
        for i = 2 to 10
            if low[i] < low
                break
            if (emUp[i] or emEq[i]) and emDw[i - 1]
                b = i - 1
                bullLevelFixed := open[b]
                bullIndexFixed := bar_index - b
                for j = b to 0
                    if open[j] > bullLevelFixed and emDw[j]
                        bullLevelFixed := open[j]
                        bullIndexFixed := bar_index - j
                if bullLevelFixed < open
                    bullLevelFixed := close > open ? high : open
                    bullIndexFixed := bar_index
                break

if high == h0 and high > h1
    if (emUp[0] or emEq[0]) and (emDw[1] or emEq[1]) and not (emEq[0] and emEq[1])
        bearLevelFixed := open
        bearIndexFixed := bar_index
    else
        for i = 2 to 10
            if high[i] > high
                break
            if (emDw[i] or emEq[i]) and emUp[i - 1]
                yb = i - 1
                bearLevelFixed := open[yb]
                bearIndexFixed := bar_index - yb
                for j = yb to 0
                    if open[j] < bearLevelFixed and emUp[j]
                        bearLevelFixed := open[j]
                        bearIndexFixed := bar_index - j
                if bearLevelFixed > open
                    bearLevelFixed := close < open ? low : open
                    bearIndexFixed := bar_index
                break

var bool bullReclaimed  = false
var int  bullReclaimBar = na
var bool bearReclaimed  = false
var int  bearReclaimBar = na

bullPeriodSweep = l0 < l1
bearPeriodSweep = h0 > h1

newBullLevel = not na(bullIndexFixed) and (na(bullIndexFixed[1]) or bullIndexFixed != bullIndexFixed[1])
if newBullLevel
    bullReclaimed  := false
    bullReclaimBar := na
if not na(bullLevelFixed) and not bullReclaimed and close > bullLevelFixed
    bullReclaimed  := true
    bullReclaimBar := bar_index
    if bullPeriodSweep
        drawEarlyCisd(true, bullLevelFixed, bullIndexFixed, bar_index)

newBearLevel = not na(bearIndexFixed) and (na(bearIndexFixed[1]) or bearIndexFixed != bearIndexFixed[1])
if newBearLevel
    bearReclaimed  := false
    bearReclaimBar := na
if not na(bearLevelFixed) and not bearReclaimed and close < bearLevelFixed
    bearReclaimed  := true
    bearReclaimBar := bar_index
    if bearPeriodSweep
        drawEarlyCisd(false, bearLevelFixed, bearIndexFixed, bar_index)

// Early C2: mark the sweep of C1 while the C2 candle is still forming. The marker
// lives for one HTF period only - at the close of the period it is cleared, and the
// confirmed setup below redraws it permanently if the candle closed back inside C1.
var bool bullSweptPeriod = false
var bool bearSweptPeriod = false
var int  periodsSeen     = 0

if periodChanged
    periodsSeen     += 1
    bullEarlySweep  := clearEarlySweep(bullEarlySweep)
    bearEarlySweep  := clearEarlySweep(bearEarlySweep)
    bullSweptPeriod := false
    bearSweptPeriod := false

// C1 must be a period that was tracked end to end, so the first (partial) period
// in the loaded history is never used as the swept candle.
earlyC2Ready = periodsSeen >= 2

if bullPeriodSweep and allowBuy and earlyC2Ready and not na(l1Bar)
    if not bullSweptPeriod
        bullSweptPeriod := true
        if showEarlyC2
            bullEarlySweep := newEarlySweep(true, l0, l0Bar, l1, l1Bar)
        if showAlerts and showEarlyC2Alerts
            alert('Bullish C2 sweep forming on ' + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    else
        bullEarlySweep := bullEarlySweep.trackExtreme(l0, l0Bar)

if bearPeriodSweep and allowSell and earlyC2Ready and not na(h1Bar)
    if not bearSweptPeriod
        bearSweptPeriod := true
        if showEarlyC2
            bearEarlySweep := newEarlySweep(false, h0, h0Bar, h1, h1Bar)
        if showAlerts and showEarlyC2Alerts
            alert('Bearish C2 sweep forming on ' + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    else
        bearEarlySweep := bearEarlySweep.trackExtreme(h0, h0Bar)

candleOffset = candleOffsetIn + 10

if periodChanged
    if htfCandles.size() > 0
        newest             = htfCandles.first()
        state.prevHigh    := newest.h
        state.prevLow     := newest.l
        state.prevHighBar := newest.hBar
        state.prevLowBar  := newest.lBar
    if htfCandles.size() > 1
        prior                  = htfCandles.get(1)
        state.prevPrevHigh    := prior.h
        state.prevPrevLow     := prior.l
        state.prevPrevHighBar := prior.hBar
        state.prevPrevLowBar  := prior.lBar
    htfCandles.unshift(newHtfCandle())
    while htfCandles.size() > htfCandleCount
        htfCandles.pop().delete()
    htfOpenBar := bar_index
    if showLH
        if hLines.size() > 0
            line.set_x2(hLines.first(), bar_index)
            line.set_x2(lLines.first(), bar_index)
        hLines.unshift(newLHLine(high))
        lLines.unshift(newLHLine(low))
        while hLines.size() > htfCandleCount
            line.delete(hLines.pop())
        while lLines.size() > htfCandleCount
            line.delete(lLines.pop())
else if htfCandles.size() > 0
    htfCandles.set(0, htfCandles.first().update(high, low, close, bar_index))

if showLH and htfCandles.size() > 0 and hLines.size() > 0
    curCandle = htfCandles.first()
    updateLHLine(hLines.first(), curCandle.h)
    updateLHLine(lLines.first(), curCandle.l)

if periodChanged
    state.prevC2Buy  := c2Buy[1]
    state.prevC2Sell := c2Sell[1]

c2BuyTrigger  = periodChanged and state.prevC2Buy
c2SellTrigger = periodChanged and state.prevC2Sell

if c2BuyTrigger and allowBuy and bullReclaimed[1]
    consumeLastEarlyCisd(bullEarlyCisdRecords)

if c2SellTrigger and allowSell and bearReclaimed[1]
    consumeLastEarlyCisd(bearEarlyCisdRecords)

buySetup  := processC2(c2BuyTrigger, allowBuy, true, state.prevLow, state.prevLowBar, state.prevPrevLow, state.prevPrevLowBar, bullLevelFixed[1], bullIndexFixed[1], bullReclaimed[1], bullReclaimBar[1], buySetup)
sellSetup := processC2(c2SellTrigger, allowSell, false, state.prevHigh, state.prevHighBar, state.prevPrevHigh, state.prevPrevHighBar, bearLevelFixed[1], bearIndexFixed[1], bearReclaimed[1], bearReclaimBar[1], sellSetup)

markTrigger(c2BuyTrigger, allowBuy, 2, true)
markTrigger(c2SellTrigger, allowSell, 2, false)

buySetup  := buySetup.extendAndCheck()
sellSetup := sellSetup.extendAndCheck()

buySetup  := buySetup.checkC4Invalid()
sellSetup := sellSetup.checkC4Invalid()

buySetup  := buySetup.checkCisdConfirm()
sellSetup := sellSetup.checkCisdConfirm()

if showAlerts
    if c2BuyTrigger and allowBuy
        alert('Bullish C2 formed on ' + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if c2SellTrigger and allowSell
        alert('Bearish C2 formed on ' + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

if showVlines and periodChanged
    vLines.unshift(line.new(bar_index, low - ta.tr, bar_index, high + ta.tr, xloc.bar_index, extend.both, lineColor, lineStyleFromStr(lineStyle), lineWidth))
    while vLines.size() > htfCandleCount
        line.delete(vLines.pop())

//#endregion

//#region [PLOT]

if (barstate.islast or barstate.isrealtime) and validTf and htfCandles.size() > 0 and not hideHtf
    n = htfCandles.size()
    for i = n - 1 to 0
        htfCandles.get(i).draw(bar_index + candleOffset + candleSpacing * (n - 1 - i))
    if showHtfOpen and not na(htfOpenBar)
        curOpenX2 = box.get_right(htfCandles.first().body)
        if na(htfOpenLn)
            htfOpenLn := line.new(htfOpenBar, currentO, curOpenX2, currentO, xloc.bar_index, extend.none, htfOpenColor, lineStyleFromStr(htfOpenStyle), htfOpenWidth)
        else
            line.set_xy1(htfOpenLn, htfOpenBar, currentO)
            line.set_xy2(htfOpenLn, curOpenX2, currentO)
            line.set_color(htfOpenLn, htfOpenColor)
            line.set_style(htfOpenLn, lineStyleFromStr(htfOpenStyle))
            line.set_width(htfOpenLn, htfOpenWidth)
    for i = n - 1 to 0
        c = htfCandles.get(i)
        if i > 0
            nextC = htfCandles.get(i - 1)
            line.set_x2(c.eqLine, nextC.midX)
        if showSweep and (c.triggerBuy or c.triggerSell) and i > 0
            nextC = htfCandles.get(i - 1)
            price = c.triggerBuy ? c.l : c.h
            if na(c.sweepLine)
                c.sweepLine := line.new(c.midX, price, nextC.midX, price, color = sweepColor, style = lineStyleFromStr(sweepStyle), width = sweepWidth)
            else
                line.set_xy1(c.sweepLine, c.midX, price)
                line.set_xy2(c.sweepLine, nextC.midX, price)
                line.set_color(c.sweepLine, sweepColor)
                line.set_style(c.sweepLine, lineStyleFromStr(sweepStyle))
                line.set_width(c.sweepLine, sweepWidth)

if (barstate.islast or barstate.isrealtime) and showStdDev and setupRecords.size() > 0
    int  nHtf     = htfCandles.size()
    bool htfShown = validTf and not hideHtf and nHtf > 0
    int  devLineX = bar_index + 2
    int  devLblX  = htfShown ? bar_index + candleOffset + candleSpacing * (nHtf - 1) + 2 + stdDevLabelGap : bar_index + 2 + stdDevLabelGap
    for rec in setupRecords
        s = rec.setup
        if not na(s) and not na(s.stdDevData)
            if not na(s.stdDevData.lines)
                for ln in s.stdDevData.lines
                    line.set_x2(ln, devLineX)
            if not na(s.stdDevData.labels)
                for lb in s.stdDevData.labels
                    label.set_x(lb, devLblX)
                    label.set_style(lb, label.style_label_left)

if barstate.islast and boolTable
    var table wm = table.new(tablePosition(tableVert, tableHorz), 1, 4,
         bgcolor      = color.new(#000000, 100),
         border_color = dashTextColor,
         border_width = 1,
         frame_color  = dashTextColor,
         frame_width  = 1)

    ltfDisp = tfLabel(ltfCode())
    htfDisp = tfLabel(autoTf)

    table.cell(wm, 0, 0, 'Expansion Model [Pro+]', text_color = dashBgColor, bgcolor = dashTextColor, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = text.align_center, text_font_family = font.family_default)

    alignBiasStr = 'Alignment : ' + ltfDisp + '-' + htfDisp + '\n\nBias : ' + biasFilter
    table.cell(wm, 0, 1, alignBiasStr, text_color = dashTextColor, bgcolor = dashBgColor, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_center, text_font_family = font.family_default)

    dateStr     = str.format_time(time_close, 'dd MMM yyyy', syminfo.timezone)
    pairDateStr = syminfo.ticker + '  |  ' + dateStr
    table.cell(wm, 0, 2, pairDateStr, text_color = dashTextColor, bgcolor = dashBgColor, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_center, text_font_family = font.family_default)

    if not validTf
        curTfStr = tfLabel(curTfCode())
        warnMsg  = '⚠ Switch to ' + ltfDisp + ' or lower (now: ' + curTfStr + ')'
        table.cell(wm, 0, 3, warnMsg, text_color = dashBgColor, bgcolor = color.new(#cc0000, 0), text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_center, text_font_family = font.family_default)

//#endregion
